      ":question/id": "6cf53d09-22eb-5e7c-8091-577208cee8a0",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "If $f(x)=\\frac{\\cos x}{1x^{2}}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x)$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}$ and $v(x)=x^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(- \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (x^{2})-(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (2 x)}{(x^{2})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{- x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 2 x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{4}}\\\\ &=\\frac{- x \\left(x \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)}{x^{4}}\\\\ &=- \\frac{x \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
